  "unresolved_entry_bank_question": "Actual first-level normal entry reads v1 through SRC0, writes v1 through DST, and restores v1 through DST before its visible bank clear. Normal bank semantics could copy between different architectural banks. The source later explicitly clears interrupted shader bank selections to use v0..255. No independent hardware guarantee about trap-entry bank reset or privileged operand override has yet been found.",
  "limits": [
    "No RuntimeEnable/SetTrapHandler call was made or observed in an experimental process; its selected runtime boolean and live TBA/TMA were not read.",
    "Module version and srcversion match the loaded module metadata, and the installed image is pinned; this is not an in-memory module-byte attestation.",
    "Current public runtime source supports interpretation of matching installed control flow but is not claimed as the complete installed source revision.",
    "Presence, selection code and trigger logic do not establish that any exception, context save, debugger event or profiling event occurred during a failing experiment.",
    "The early-entry bank question remains conditional on actual trap-mode operand semantics and trap activation; it is not a proven corruption mechanism."
